INSERT INTO stories (id, date, month, summary_en, html_en, source_url, published) VALUES ('2026-01-01-portugal-b2g-sme-extension', '2026-01-01', '2026-01', 'Portugal''s structured B2G e-invoicing mandate now applies to small, medium, and micro-enterprises, not just large companies — while the separate PDF signature requirement has been pushed back a full year via the 2026 State Budget.', '<h3>🇵🇹 Portugal''s B2G mandate extends to SMEs, while the PDF deadline gets a reprieve</h3>
<p>From today, Portugal''s structured e-invoicing requirement for public-sector suppliers — issuing invoices in the national CIUS-PT format, an EN 16931-based specification, via the eSPap-operated FE-AP platform — extends beyond large companies to small, medium, and micro-enterprises. This closes a gap that''s existed since 2021, when the mandate first took effect for large suppliers only.</p>
<p>Worth being clear about what this doesn''t change: Portugal still has no general B2B or B2C e-invoicing mandate. Paper and PDF invoices remain valid outside the public-sector context. What does apply universally, regardless of company size or B2G status, is a separate layer that''s easy to overlook precisely because it''s been in force so long it barely gets discussed: certified invoicing software (mandatory since 2010–2011), an ATCUD unique document code, and a QR code on every invoice. Using uncertified software doesn''t create a compliance gap to fix later — it makes the invoice invalid outright.</p>
<p>Separately, and confirmed via the 2026 State Budget approved in late November 2025, the requirement for a Qualified Electronic Signature (QES) on PDF invoices — originally planned for this year — has been deferred a full year, to 1 January 2027. Until 31 December 2026, PDF invoices issued by certified software with ATCUD and a QR code remain valid without one.</p>
<p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you supply any Portuguese public-sector body and don''t yet issue structured CIUS-PT invoices, that''s now a live compliance gap rather than something to plan around later. And regardless of B2G status, it''s worth confirming your invoicing software is genuinely on the AT-certified list — this is the requirement most likely to catch a business out precisely because it long predates the more visible 2026/2027 headlines.</p>', 'https://www.portaldasfinancas.gov.pt/pt/menu.action?pai=5075', 1);
